# oracle: fix qeq/fire, small coul/long system with example param.qeq2, run 0 + 10 nve
# oracle-inputs: w36qeq_param.qeq2
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): pe 1.5e-15; atoms 7.2e-16. Source: src/QEQ/fix_qeq.cpp (setup_pre_force), fix_qeq_point.cpp, fix_qeq_dynamic.cpp, fix_qeq_fire.cpp at b332f28; the step-0 gap of 7e-8 was the kspace G-ewald re-chosen after the solve.
units metal
atom_style charge
boundary p p p
region box block 0 20 0 20 0 20
create_box 2 box
create_atoms 1 single 5.0 5.0 5.0
create_atoms 2 single 7.5 5.0 5.0
create_atoms 1 single 10.0 5.0 5.0
create_atoms 2 single 5.0 7.5 5.0
create_atoms 1 single 7.5 7.5 5.0
create_atoms 2 single 10.0 7.5 5.0
mass 1 28.0855
mass 2 15.9999
set atom 1 charge -0.5
set atom 2 charge 0.5
set atom 3 charge -0.5
set atom 4 charge 0.5
set atom 5 charge -0.5
set atom 6 charge 0.5
pair_style coul/long 8.0
pair_coeff * *
kspace_style pppm 1.0e-6
neighbor 1.0 bin
fix q all qeq/fire 1 8 1.0e-10 100000 w36qeq_param.qeq2
fix 1 all nve
compute qa all property/atom q
compute qs all reduce sum c_qa
compute qm all reduce max c_qa
thermo_style custom step pe c_qs c_qm
thermo_modify format float %.15g
thermo 5
timestep 0.0001
velocity all create 300.0 1281937
run 0
run 10
